sdl2: on X11, keep the keyboard grab only while the pointer is over the window

On X11 SDL implements the focus keyboard grab with an active keyboard grab.
Holding it after the pointer left the window kept the desktop's panel menus
and popups from taking the keyboard: Cinnamon's menu opened with typing going
to the guest, applets needed a second click, and a notification popup could
stay stuck open. The grab now also needs the pointer over the window on X11,
as in virt-viewer, and the title only offers Ctrl+Alt+G while it is held.

SDL can keep a stale pointer focus from a crossing made while a dialog had the
focus, so the check asks the X server where the pointer is. The absolute
pointer grab taken when focus returns uses the same check: an X11 grab
confines the pointer to the window, so grabbing on a stale position pulled the
pointer into the window. Wayland keeps both grabs as before.

diff --git i/ui/sdl2.c w/ui/sdl2.c
index b87dde3..a49b9af 100644
--- i/ui/sdl2.c
+++ w/ui/sdl2.c
@@ -203,6 +203,35 @@ static bool focus_keyboard_grab;
  */
 static bool keyboard_released;
 
+/*
+ * On X11 a keyboard grab is an active grab: while it is held, the panel's
+ * menus and popups cannot take the keyboard, so after the pointer leaves the
+ * window they open with their input going to the guest, or get stuck open.
+ * There the grab follows the pointer as well as focus, as in virt-viewer: the
+ * keyboard goes to the guest while the window has focus and the pointer is
+ * over it.  Wayland's keyboard shortcuts inhibitor needs no such care.
+ */
+static bool sdl_x11_pointer_outside(struct sdl2_console *scon)
+{
+    int x, y, win_x, win_y, win_w, win_h;
+
+    if (g_strcmp0(SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver(), "x11") != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (SDL_GetMouseFocus() != scon->real_window) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    /*
+     * SDL can keep the pointer focus from a crossing made while another
+     * window, such as a dialog, had the focus.  Ask the server where the
+     * pointer really is before taking the keyboard.
+     */
+    SDL_GetGlobalMouseState(&x, &y);
+    SDL_GetWindowPosition(scon->real_window, &win_x, &win_y);
+    SDL_GetWindowSize(scon->real_window, &win_w, &win_h);
+    return x < win_x || y < win_y || x >= win_x + win_w || y >= win_y + win_h;
+}
